    "kjScale": {
      "page": "current",
      "text": "kJ circle sizing\n\n1. Area, not radius: r = 175px × √(kJ ÷ 1,300). Twice the work = twice the disc area.\n\n2. One fixed scale every day, anchored to the biggest planned ride (1,300 kJ long climb = 175px, nearly full width).\n   300 kJ → 84px · 312 → 86px · 600 → 119px · 653 → 124px · 1,300 → 175px\n\n3. Target ring uses the same formula. Over or under = the gap between disc and dashed ring (partial day: 312 inside 600 → a 33px gap).\n\n4. Shared with calories: 1 kJ of ride work ≈ 1 kcal burned, so a 653 kJ disc and a 653 kcal meal would be the same size.\n\n5. Input is real work only: kJ = avg power × moving time ÷ 1000. Never Strava calories. No power data → empty ring, no guessed fill.\n\n6. Over the scale (>1,300 kJ): let it bleed off the edges, or re-anchor to the season's biggest planned day before you get there.",
      "w": 380,
      "x": 470,
      "y": 0
    },
